wn exactly which categories and value range to draw. Here category `F` has no data and still gets an empty slot, and the Y range stays `[0, 40]` even though the largest bar is 30 - handy when several charts need to share a scale."],[1807,"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin the visible range. Use them to keep a fixed scale, or to keep several charts comparable."],[1798,"`xGridlines` and `yGridlines` add faint lines across the plot so it is easier to read a value back off an axis."],[1859,"`xl` - Extra large spacing"],[1800,"`xLabels` and `yLabels` toggle the tick labels on each axis. Turn them off for sparklines or when the surrounding UI already names the values."],[1808,"`xNice` and `yNice` round the domain out to friendlier numbers (e.g. 0.2 to 1.0), so ticks land on values people expect."],[1811,"`xPaddingOuter` and `yPaddingOuter` add breathing room at the ends of a band or point scale so the first and last values are not pinned to the edges."],[1855,"`xs` - Extra small spacing"],[1663,"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - abbreviated dates on one axis, thousands separators on the other. The functions receive the raw accessor value, so they also cover currency, units, or percentages."],[1804,"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - dates, currency, units, percentages - and the tooltip follows the same formatting."],[1801,"`xTickMarks` and `yTickMarks` draw the short lines at each tick value, which helps tie a label to its exact position on the axis."],[1799,"`xTitle` and `yTitle` label what each axis actually measures, e.g. \"Month\" and \"Temperature (°F)\"."],[1809,"`xZero` and `yZero` stretch the domain to include zero. Worth doing when the absolute size of the values matters, not just their movement."],[1694,"✅ Custom domains"],[1695,"✅ Design system alignment"],[1270,"✅ For binary on/off preferences (e.g. Wi-Fi, notifications, dark mode)"],[1525,"✅ For compact action grouping — related actions in space-constrained layouts (e.g. U